Subject: [PATCH] Report reference diagnostics at each literal operand start


diff --git a/audit/reference-contract.md b/audit/reference-contract.md
index 84f262ad107a7d3cf7218af24ce9ab8fe396862f..af86a7eb63db713635080a3a287c31b3053d5203 100644
--- a/audit/reference-contract.md
+++ b/audit/reference-contract.md
@@ -153,3 +153,21 @@ The result therefore keeps `native_execution_authenticated`,
 `retail_runtime_compatibility_verified`, `runtime_validation_passed`,
 `owner_acceptance` and `package_ready` false. They are separate evidentiary gates;
 the encoded-reference result itself can become true when its stated proof succeeds.
+
+## Review correction: literal operand positions
+
+Review of source commit `bfa2d4af` found that the second animation string's
+diagnostic used the cursor after reading the string. With `tree\0` followed by
+an encrypted `anim` string, it reported stack offset 24 instead of the operand's
+start at 18. A regression reproduced the failure. Literal decoding now captures
+the cursor before reading; the instruction span remains exactly 13 through 24.
+The analogous audit also replaced the general instruction stack position with
+each string's actual start for switch rows/default sentinels and indirect field
+literals. Function/namespace token readers already saved their start correctly.
+
+The source-only reference suite now has 19 passing methods, including the
+animation, switch and indirect-field position regressions and both retained
+Beacon inputs. The original source observation JSON keeps its initial reader
+hash as historical evidence; the corrected reader reproduces the same Beacon
+references, counts and qualification observations. No native run or archive
+finalization is implied by this diagnostic correction.
